languages/structure.md:3:13: personified-verb: "The quote" is not a person or a program and cannot "say"; make the program or person that acts the subject, or use a verb such as "holds", "marks", "declares" or "determines"
languages/structure.md:3:18: placeholder-noun: "what it is" is a free relative clause; name the exact term instead, such as "the element type" or "the verb's symbol"
languages/structure.md:3:23: self-reference: the sentence ends on "it is", which points back at its own subject "The quote"; end on the new fact instead
languages/structure.md:11:14: personified-verb: "The value" is not a person or a program and cannot "decide"; make the program or person that acts the subject, or use a verb such as "holds", "marks", "declares" or "determines"
